================================================================================
METHODS
================================================================================

Implementing a published method is not reproducing the document that
describes it, and the standards below are cited, not redistributed. Consult
the originals for authoritative wording:

  CIE S 011            standard general skies
  Perez et al. (1993)  all-weather sky model
  Perez et al. (1990)  luminous efficacy (simplified fit)
  Tregenza & Reinhart  sky subdivision
  NOAA Solar Calculator, after Meeus — solar position
  BRE and BS 8206-2    split-flux components, average daylight factor
  Nabil & Mardaljevic (2005) — useful daylight illuminance
  IES LM-83            sDA and ASE (indicative only; blind operation is not
                       modelled, so results are not LM-83 submissions)
